--
Clang's type trait `__reference_binds_to_temporary(T, U)' (true when a
reference of type T initialized from an expression of type U binds to a
materialized temporary, [dcl.init.ref]/5.4) is not known to the front end
("symbol '__reference_binds_to_temporary' is unknown").  libc++'s <tuple>
uses it in `__tuple_leaf::__can_bind_reference' (a static_assert guard in
the leaf's converting constructor), so tuple and map construction under
libc++ drop that member (audit residue item 10, round 162).  The trait is
a type predicate over two types and belongs with the other Clang/GCC type
traits (`__is_convertible' & co.).
